A note from the maintainer, before the license text below: this license covers Pi Forensics
Suite's own original source code only. This project installs, imports, vendors, or loads a
large number of pre-existing third-party forensic tools, Python libraries, and frontend
assets to do its job - each of those keeps its own separate license, and none of them are
covered by, or become subject to, the MIT terms below. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the
full list, including a few licenses that are worth reading closely because they aren't
standard open-source terms (notably MVT, Volatility 3, and SQLite Dissect).

License history: this project started life under this same MIT license (its very first
commit, 2026-08-05), was switched to GPLv3 two days later, then briefly to Apache License
2.0 (2026-09-04, for commercial/patent-grant reasons), and back to MIT the same day for
simplicity, matching this project's own stated audience (students, hobbyists, and low-budget
users) more than a longer, more formal license would - reversible again if that changes.

